@Steve L

What's being discussed here is the phenomenon of "transcreation" - "translating" film titles in such a way as to improve their marketability, though it is frequently nonsensical.

Countries with a high foreign-language-literacy rate (like in Scandinavia vis a vis English) tend to do it much less.

From my own experience - Israel, Austria, Japan - it is extremely rare to go to the movies and have the film's original title accurately translated.

